1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,749
The second benefit is of course manifestation because number one when you're gentling to manifest first you just need to write down your desires.
第二个好处，作者认为是“显化”。她说，首先写下愿望；gentling 为待听辨字幕。

2
00:00:07,759 --> 00:00:14,840
Just that very practice of clarifying what is it that I want and why do I want that is going to putut so much into perspective for you.
仅仅澄清“我想要什么，为什么想要”，作者就觉得能让许多事情变得更清楚。

3
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:20,319
And remove any outside noise or focusing on things that you think you want or that other people have because it looks cool.
也能排除外界的干扰，不再只关注自己以为想要、或别人有而看起来很酷的东西。

4
00:00:20,319 --> 00:00:25,079
But that doesn't really align with your personal vision or where you want to be or what your purpose is.
那些东西也许并不符合你的个人愿景、想去的方向或人生目的。

5
00:00:25,079 --> 00:00:33,759
When you are taking time to put yourself in a certain experience or to wish for something that you want that's when you can fully understand all aspects of that desire.
当你花时间想象某个经历，或期盼想要的东西，就能更全面地理解那个愿望。

6
00:00:33,759 --> 00:00:37,199
And therefore make it even easier to bring it into your life.
作者认为，这样也更容易把它带进自己的生活。

7
00:00:37,199 --> 00:00:46,199
On top of that ging also helps rewire your conscious mind just because of this process of repeatedly writing about your goals about your manifestations your desires.
此外，作者认为不断写目标、愿景和愿望能重塑意识；ging 为不确定字幕。

8
00:00:46,199 --> 00:00:54,949
As you're writing about them you're also forcing your mind to visualize yourself living them out and imagining what it would be like if you got that best case scenario.
写的时候，也是在让自己想象实现目标后的生活，想象最理想的情况。

9
00:00:54,959 --> 00:01:03,160
Journaling can really help create this emotional alignment which is so necessary and probably and honestly the most important part of manifestation I think.
作者认为，日记能帮助形成“情绪一致”，并把这视为显化中非常重要的一部分。

10
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:08,920
Don't do anything else don't even make a vision board as long as you are aligning your emotions you are going to manifest like this.
她说，甚至不用做愿景板，只要情绪一致就会显化；这是她的个人主张。

11
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:17,400
And because you're journaling and writing pages I'm talking pages of you living out your dream life you have never felt it or visualized it stronger.
当你一页又一页地写自己过着理想生活时，作者说那种感受和想象会格外强烈。

12
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:22,749
Because you're really immersing yourself in that experience by like writing the story of you living it out.
因为你通过写故事，让自己沉浸在实现愿望的经历中。

13
00:01:22,759 --> 00:01:27,480
It's not just about writing a list of I wish this would happen for me I hope this happens.
不只是列出“我希望这发生在我身上”“希望这能成真”。

14
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:35,519
It's writing the story of this is how I live this is how I feel in the morning this is what's happened to me since I got this and life is better than ever.
而是写“我这样生活，早上这样感受；得到它后发生了这些事，生活比以前更好”。

15
00:01:35,519 --> 00:01:38,120
This is how I feel about myself about the world.
再写自己怎样看待自己，以及怎样看待世界。

16
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:46,440
And in that process your mindset is also being rewired because you are taking out all of that gunk and junk of self doubt and negative thoughts and thinking that you're not going to get anything.
在这个过程中，作者认为心态也会改变，因为你正在清理自我怀疑、负面想法和“我不会得到什么”的念头。

17
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:56,600
Because now your brain is so used to this process of seeing yourself live out your dream life because you're actually taking time to normalize that idea to your brain as you journal about it.
作者说，因为你反复想象自己实现理想生活，写下来会让大脑逐渐觉得这种生活很正常。

18
00:01:56,600 --> 00:02:02,040
So we've got growth manifestation rewiring your mind and the fourth benefit is inspiration.
所以，前面说了成长、显化和改变心态，第四个好处是灵感。

19
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:12,230
Journaling is such a great tool to be able to clear out your mind to allow more positive things to come into it which will give you ideas and inspiration on your next steps forward.
作者认为日记能清理思路，容纳更多积极的东西，给下一步带来想法和灵感。

20
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:17,509
You can find out your purpose you can find out what you really want to do you can tap into those subconscious thoughts.
你可以发现自己的目的、真正想做什么，并接触那些潜藏的想法。

21
00:02:17,519 --> 00:02:22,670
Because every single day we are picking up so much more noise and thoughts and stresses from everything around us.
因为每天，我们都会从周遭接收到很多杂音、想法和压力。

22
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:33,910
Whether it be our work environment people worries that we have that come up dayt day and it's blocking us from actually accessing all of the thoughts and inspiration that we already have.
工作环境、人际和每天的担忧，作者认为都可能阻挡我们接触已有的想法和灵感。

23
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:41,600
Just by writing about something you're going through already you can start tapping into new ideas and problem solving techniques to get past it.
仅仅写一写正在经历的事情，就可能帮助你产生新想法和解决问题的方法，跨过它。

24
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:46,280
And then the last benefit of journaling is self lov improving the relationship you have with yourself.
最后一个好处，作者称为“自爱”，即改善与自己的关系。

25
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:51,560
Building up your self esteem because of the way that you do your shadow work or the prompts that you are writing about.
通过作者所说的“阴影工作”或写作提示，建立自尊。

26
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:57,440
Or the way that you are reframing any worries or stresses that you have about yourself because you're taking the time to write about it.
也可以把关于自己的担忧和压力重新换个角度理解，因为你花时间把它们写下来。

27
00:02:57,440 --> 00:03:03,079
Journaling will encourage your self awareness when you are actually really focusing on why am I going through this.
作者认为，日记能增强自我觉察，因为你认真思考“我为什么经历这些”。

28
00:03:03,079 --> 00:03:10,600
Or even considering other perspectives while you're journaling because you're deep diving into a particular situation to really understand it more.
写作时还可以考虑其他角度，深入某个具体情况，以更好地理解它。

29
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:13,199
It creates emotional balance and self acceptance.
作者认为这会带来情绪平衡和自我接纳。

30
00:03:13,199 --> 00:03:21,360
Okay now that we've gone through all the benefits I want you to pick one or two maximum three benefits that you want to gain from journaling.
说完这些好处，我想让你选一个或两个，最多三个，作为写日记希望得到的东西。

31
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:27,120
Maybe you want to manifest while also rewire your mind if you're someone who tends to think really negatively or doubt yourself.
也许你想显化，同时改变思维方式，尤其当你容易消极思考或怀疑自己。

32
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:32,000
And then we're really going to create a strategy that helps you journal in that way every single day.
接着，我们要制定一个策略，帮助你每天按选定的方式写日记。
